/*******************************************************
 * ANDROID NOTIFICATIONS – THEORY
 *
 * -----------------------------------------------------
 * WHAT IS A NOTIFICATION?
 * -----------------------------------------------------
 * • A notification is a system-level UI message.
 * • It appears outside the app (status bar / tray).
 * • It can be shown even when the app is closed.
 *
 * -----------------------------------------------------
 * WHY NOTIFICATIONS ARE USED
 * -----------------------------------------------------
 * • Inform users about important events
 * • Background updates
 * • Messages / Alerts / Reminders
 *
 * Real-world Examples:
 * • WhatsApp new message
 * • Email received
 * • Download completed
 * • Payment alert
 *
 * -----------------------------------------------------
 * ANDROID NOTIFICATION FLOW
 * -----------------------------------------------------
 *
 * App Code
 *   ↓
 * NotificationCompat.Builder
 *   ↓
 * NotificationManager / NotificationManagerCompat
 *   ↓
 * Android System UI
 *   ↓
 * Status Bar / Notification Drawer
 *
 * -----------------------------------------------------
 * IMPORTANT ANDROID RULES
 * -----------------------------------------------------
 *
 * ANDROID 8+ (API 26):
 * • Notification CHANNEL is mandatory
 * • Without channel → app crashes / no notification
 *
 * ANDROID 13+ (API 33):
 * • POST_NOTIFICATIONS permission is required
 * • Runtime permission (like camera/location)
 *
 * -----------------------------------------------------
 * CORE COMPONENTS
 * -----------------------------------------------------
 *
 * 1️⃣ Notification Channel
 *    - Controls sound, vibration, importance
 *
 * 2️⃣ Notification Permission
 *    - User must allow notifications explicitly
 *
 * 3️⃣ Notification ID
 *    - Same ID → update notification
 *    - Different ID → multiple notifications
 *
 * 4️⃣ Priority / Importance
 *    - LOW / DEFAULT / HIGH
 *
 * -----------------------------------------------------
 * BEST PRACTICES
 * -----------------------------------------------------
 * • Always create channel before sending notification
 * • Always use NotificationCompat (backward compatible)
 * • Always provide small icon
 * • Keep notification text short & clear
 *
 *******************************************************/
